#
# Vtable.HRDPS -- ECCC HRDPS continental 2.5 km, GRIB2 (one field per file on
# the MSC Datamart). Codes read from the files themselves (2026-11-13):
#   isobaric TMP 0/0/0, HGT 0/3/5, RH 0/1/1, UGRD 0/2/2, VGRD 0/2/3 at level 100;
#   2 m TMP/RH and 10 m UGRD/VGRD at 103; PRES_Sfc 0/3/0 @1; PRMSL 0/3/1 @101;
#   HGT_Sfc 0/3/5 @1; SKINT 0/0/17 @1; SNOD 0/1/11 @1; SDWE 0/1/60 @1;
#   TSOIL 2/0/2 (@106 0-0.1 m, and @1 as TSOIL_Sfc); SOILW 2/0/25 @106 0-0.01 / 0-0.1 m.
# Soil: ECCC publishes only two shallow moisture layers and one temperature
# layer plus the soil surface, so real.exe interpolates Noah's four layers from
# 0-1 / 0-10 cm (SM) and 0 / 0-10 cm (ST). HRDPS has no LANDSEA or SEAICE
# field: the land mask comes from geogrid, sea ice is absent (none in the PNW
# soaring season). RH is used for moisture (SPFH also exists). The GRIB1
# columns are nominal; ungrib matches on the GRIB2 columns.
